From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: no macOS prompt for the full-grab tap at the VM's start

What: setFullGrab makes the full-grab event tap only when macOS already lets
OmacVM control the computer (CGPreflightPostEventAccess, an answer without a
prompt; Accessibility's answer when there is no entry of its own). Without
it: no CGEventTapCreate, qemu.log says "Could not create event tap" as before
(OmacVM.app's window note reads it) and why.

Why: CGEventTapCreate for an app that is not allowed is refused anyway, and
macOS 27 shows "<app> would like to control this Mac ... Open System Settings
/ Deny" for it (tccd: "Notifying for access kTCCServicePostEvent ... Service
kTCCServicePostEvent does not allow prompting; returning denied"). That came
at every VM start, also with nobody at the Mac: 54 such dialogs in 36 hours on
the test Mac mini (test copies under bundle ids without a grant), and every
VM start for a person who has not turned OmacVM on (the app clears an old
entry once per launch, a Deny with it: KeyAccess.clearOldEntryOnce). OmacVM.app
asks only when the person clicks Allow... in the VM window (KeyAccess.request:
CGRequestPostEventAccess and the Accessibility pane).

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's own rule on top of the full-grab patches).

Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-tap-no-ask.sh (CI: omacvm_tap_allowed from
this patch with made-up answers; the runtime build: also that setFullGrab asks
it before its only CGEventTapCreate). Applies after omacvm-cocoa-keys-last.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -2186,12 +2186,35 @@
     return v && !strcmp(v, "1") ? kCGTailAppendEventTap : kCGHeadInsertEventTap;
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the full-grab tap is made only when macOS already lets OmacVM
+ * control the computer (CGPreflightPostEventAccess: an answer, no prompt).
+ * Without that, CGEventTapCreate is refused anyway, and macOS shows "... would
+ * like to control this Mac" for it at every VM start (tccd: "Notifying for
+ * access kTCCServicePostEvent"), also while nobody is at the Mac. OmacVM.app
+ * asks only from Allow... in the VM window (KeyAccess.request). qemu.log
+ * still says "Could not create event tap", which the window's note reads.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_tap_allowed(void)
+{
+    if (CGPreflightPostEventAccess()) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    info_report("cocoa: not allowed to control the computer: no full-grab tap, "
+                "and no macOS prompt at the start (Allow... in the VM window asks)");
+    return false;
+}
+
 - (void) setFullGrab:(id)sender
 {
     COCOA_DEBUG("QemuCocoaView: setFullGrab\n");
 
     CGEventMask mask = CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyDown) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyUp) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventFlagsChanged);
     CGEventTapPlacement place = omacvm_keys_place();
+    if (!omacvm_tap_allowed()) {
+        warn_report("Could not create event tap, system key combos will not be captured.\n");
+        return;
+    }
     eventsTap = CGEventTapCreate(kCGHIDEventTap, place, kCGEventTapOptionDefault,
                                  mask, handleTapEvent, self);
     if (!eventsTap) {
